      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see, so each driver is responsible for the optimization? One of the reasons for this approach I have here is that it aligns with Zephyr\u0027s upstream drivers. Looking at the two appraoches I\u0027m seeing:\n\n- If each driver checks CONFIG_SENSOR_INTERRUPT_THRESHOLD (or some variation of that config name) in their `set_data_rate` implementation we\u0027re going to replicate the same logic.\n- Doing the same calculation in motionsense makes it so the calculation/decision of turning interrupts on/off is in one place. It will require one unit test (instead of one per driver). And if we find a bug, it\u0027ll be easy to fix for all boards.\n- Having some alignment here makes it easier when we move to the upstream drivers which offer a way to turn on/off interrupts.",
      "parentUuid": "eb2ca254_d0a4a140",
